  "version": 3,
  "status": "registered",
  "title": "Uniform-constant Erd\u0151s unit-distance conjecture is false",
  "abstract": "For every C > 0 and every N there exist n \u2265 N and an n-point set P \u2286 \u211d\u00b2 whose number of unit-distance pairs exceeds n^(1 + C / log log n). This refutes Erd\u0151s's 1946 conjectured bound \u03bd(n) \u2264 n^(1 + C/log log n) for an absolute constant C. The theorem quantifies over C > 0; this is harmless because any bound with C \u2264 0 would imply the corresponding bound for a positive C.\n",
